<title>DUBAI: Gulf states 1996 oil revenues seen at $90 billion.</title>
<headline>Gulf states 1996 oil revenues seen at $90 billion.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1996-12-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Higher world oil prices will lift Gulf Arab states' oil revenue to some $90 billion this year from $78 billion in 1995, Emirates Industrial Bank said on Sunday.</p>
<p>&quot;(This) will contribute to a decrease in budget deficits and encourage the economic positions in these countries in general,&quot; the bank said in its latest economic bulletin.</p>
<p>The oil-rich Gulf Cooperation Council GCC is made up of Saudi Arabia -- the world's biggest crude producer and exporter -- Kuwait, United Arab Emirates, Qatar, Bahrain and Oman.</p>
<p>Oil is currently trading around its highest level since the 1991 Gulf War.</p>
</text>
